Instruction
===========

You have to edit the .sh files to reflect your settings:

HIVE_TABLE	= the table in Hive you want to create
HBASE_TABLE 	= the HBase table you want to create
IMPALA_HOST 	= the hostname and port of your Impala Server is running on (HOST:PORT)
IMPALA_OPTS 	= additional switches you want to pass to impala-shell 
		  (-k for kerberos as example)


Background on novatechflow.com:
- Historical Impala Setup on RHEL 6 with Kerberos (Impala 0.3 Era)
  https://www.novatechflow.com/2012/12/impala-and-kerberos.html
- Using Hive's HBaseStorageHandler with Existing HBase Tables
  https://www.novatechflow.com/2012/12/using-hives-hbase-handler.html
